  "reason": "Format 13 is unchanged. The wall clock's rule for which exact readings are valid now lives in an accumulator that a fresh read and a recording's extension share; a test checks that it keeps the readings the previous loop kept, on every prefix of random clocks set, stepped and unset. Entry selection, plausibility, the seconds view of the readings and filename zones are unchanged. A loaded log keeps its UTC mapping, a recording extends its clock readings, and the log data interface gains that mapping; REV parsing, decoding, sample retention and synchronization do not read it, so cached synchronizations give the same answers.",
